      "q": "What is the value of $\\frac{5.4(0.1 \\times 0.1 \\times 0.1 + 0.03 \\times 0.03 \\times 0.03)}{(0.3 \\times 0.3 \\times 0.3 + 0.09 \\times 0.09 \\times 0.09)}$?",
      "options": [
        "0.5",
        "0.2",
        "0.4",
        "0.6"
      ],
      "correct": 1,
      "explain": "Let $a = 0.1$ and $b = 0.03$. \nThe numerator is $5.4(a^3 + b^3)$. \nThe denominator has terms $(3a)^3 + (3b)^3 = 27a^3 + 27b^3 = 27(a^3 + b^3)$.\nSo, the expression simplifies to $\\frac{5.4(a^3 + b^3)}{27(a^3 + b^3)} = \\frac{5.4}{27} = 0.2$.",
